From 479b9dd3a4730484ffca3d875797d3ce3c6c88bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ender Hsieh <andhsieh@nvidia.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 23:51:37 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] port: look up port metrics through a table

Replace the metricName if/else chains in the Fabric switch and network
adapter port metrics handlers with a name-to-JSON-pointer table, so
adding a counter is one table row rather than another branch.

Tested: Ran the bmcweb unit-test CI locally against this change: build,
69/69 unit tests, and clang-tidy all pass.

1. The mapping is unchanged - every D-Bus metric name and every Redfish
   JSON pointer in the two tables matches the branch it replaces.
2. No Redfish output change is expected; this is a refactor of the
   decode step only.

Change-Id: I19867ea60b27eaef58f51bf5857955c9cebe68d9
Signed-off-by: Ender Hsieh <andhsieh@nvidia.com>
---
 redfish-core/lib/network_adapter.hpp | 135 ++++++---------------------
 redfish-core/lib/switch_port.hpp     |  82 +++++++---------
 2 files changed, 61 insertions(+), 156 deletions(-)

